  "problem": "Inferred scientific statements could be treated as literal observations. Stale approvals, incomplete source runs or changed field hashes could promote. Rollback could destroy newer attempt history. Automated rules could be treated as source-access or legal authorization. Editing sealed normalization or identity sources would break WP7/normalization artifact seals.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Promotion classes live in packages/enrichment/promotion.mjs. Validated literal publisher metadata can promote under an approved field/source rule without a click per field. Inferred scientific statements, identity merges and ambiguous mappings cannot receive literal-observation status. Stale approvals, incomplete source runs and changed field hashes cannot promote; unaffected accepted claims remain available. Rollback restores prior public facts and retains newer attempt/review history. Scientific and technical acceptance are separate. Automated rules cannot authorize source access or legal rights. Last-good generation remains live-2026-09-03-85b50522b420. Sealed packages/normalization/src and packages/identity/src/review-ledger.mjs are unchanged.",
